Z||000000||HYPTNOTiSE||06-26-2000||02:50 PM||||I know chris west west makes a good looking set of headers in stainless priced at 700 bucks. I'm most likely going to get these but do any of you have any other suggestions.<P>I can't get ahold of fiero heaven.<BR>Dare i ask...What about FOCOA headers?<BR>Fiero store sprint manifolds are too pricy for my neeeds.  <P>I need something that is close to a Tuned header as possible. I wonder if i could have someone locally build me a set for under 700.<P>Mike LeCompte||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||06-26-2000||03:27 PM||||get ready for 100 posts!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||CUTTER||06-26-2000||05:17 PM||||What don headers do? I mean they dont give to much of a HP gain and they are exspensive. Is it worh $700?||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||06-26-2000||05:41 PM||||Better check out 1FSTsM6's header results before spending 700 bucks...||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||06-26-2000||08:44 PM||||Port out your stock manifolds. It’s the best bang for the buck and an easy 8-10 hp gain. The difference between ported manifolds and headers is about 2-4 hp and $650 out of your pocket. Not worth it in my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||06-26-2000||08:47 PM||||Tuned headers,and unequal-length(stock-type) tube headers are two different things.<BR>I might consider a set of stainless headers for my TDC motor,as a future upgrade,too much $ for now,however.<BR>Might give around 15 horsepower,depending on what other mods you have done.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||06-26-2000||09:02 PM||||I'm with 88formula on this one!! I ported my manifolds because of the same reasons stated<BR>I had heard 8-15hp gain with the port job and the same gains with headers. I did have a exhaust leak so while they were off..why not?<P>I think the headers are more for looks than true HP. F/S (words) sprint performance manifolds, No were does it say HEADER??<P>Is it worth it?  I don't know, I just have something else to do with my $700.00  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||HYPTNOTiSE||06-27-2000||12:13 AM||||Ok guys, thanks, and i was starting to think about it myself, 700 bucks is alot of money!!! especially for a gain of 5+ hp over my ported exhuast manifolds.  I mean 700 bucks is about 1/4 of the way to a blower! and that's like 60+ hp!  Do you think a tuned equal length header on a highly modifed 3.2 pushing 230+hp would be worth 700? It would sure look awesome! But i get the point...||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||06-27-2000||12:33 PM||||unless you have a 3.4 liter don't waste your money. I payed $522 for the headers from Chris West then $200 for Jet Hot coating and LOST LOT of torque... the increse in HP was there but not at a useable RPM.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno_1.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||1
